A class is a blueprint for objects. An object is an instance of that class and can access its fields and methods.

```java
class Car {
    String model;
    void drive() { System.out.println(model + " is driving"); }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Car car = new Car();
        car.model = "Camry";
        car.drive();
    }
}
```

